<meta type=article>
  <title | Cross-reference test fixture>
  <author | Ariel Balter>
</meta>

<config ref-prefix-eqn="Eq.">

<section | Equations with various numbering states>

A numbered labeled equation:

<$$ #eqn:newton | F = ma $$>

A numbered unlabeled equation:

<$$ | E = mc^2 $$>

An unnumbered labeled equation (uses -numbered boolean kwarg):

<$$ #eqn:energy -numbered | H = T + V $$>

An unnumbered labeled equation (uses numbered=false kwarg form):

<$$ #eqn:alt-form numbered=false | x + y = z $$>

An unnumbered unlabeled equation:

<$$ -numbered | a = b $$>


<section | References to equations>

Reference to numbered labeled with config prefix override (renders "Eq. 1"): see <ref @eqn:newton>.

Reference to numbered labeled without override would use default prefix. The second equation has no label and cannot be referenced. The third is unnumbered labeled (renders label-tail "energy"): see <ref @eqn:energy>.

Reference to a second unnumbered labeled (renders "alt-form"): see <ref @eqn:alt-form>.

Reference to missing label (produces error): <ref @eqn:nonexistent>.


<section | Figures>

A figure with a colon-id and caption:

<figure #fig:elephant src="assets/elephant.jpg" | An African elephant photographed in Tanzania.>

A figure without a label (gets auto-number, not referenceable):

<figure src="assets/scatter-regression.svg" | A scatter plot (stand-in for a second numbered figure).>

A figure with -numbered (no visible label, not in numbered sequence):

<figure #fig:lion -numbered src="assets/elephant.jpg" | Another elephant (stand-in for an unnumbered labeled figure).>

Reference to numbered figure (renders "figure 1"): see <ref @fig:elephant>.


<section | Notes>

A labeled endnote<note #note:galton placement=foot | Galton coined the term "regression" in 1886 while studying the heights of parents and their adult children.> demonstrating a colon-id note.

An unlabeled note<note | This note has no id and cannot be cross-referenced.> demonstrating auto-id behavior.

Reference to labeled note (renders "note 1"): see <ref @note:galton>.


<section | Edge cases>

A numbered equation with an unregistered prefix (id prefix "custom" is not in the prefix dictionary):

<$$ #custom:thing | x = y $$>

Reference to an id with a colon but an unregistered prefix (renders just the number, no word): <ref @custom:thing>.

Reference to an id without a colon — not in the label index (produces error): <ref @not-a-label>.

Reference with no id at all (produces error): <ref>.
